      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When timing is erratic, think about parasitic loads or external fluctuations affecting the control system. A failing contactor or relay, which manages the power cycles, can often behave erratically under load. Furthermore, electromagnetic interference (EMI) from nearby equipment or power surges can cause momentary hiccups in sensitive electronic controls. A specialized technician should test the contactors with an oscilloscope to pinpoint these transient electrical events.",
